course: dictionary
lesson: 12342
title: Crabs: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word crabs can mean a sea animal, or it can mean the food made from that animal. The words around it show you which meaning the writer chose.
explain: «Mia lifted a crab from the rock pool and put it back.» You lift an animal and put it back, so here crabs are animals. «We had crab legs for dinner by the sea.» You eat food, so here crabs means food.
explain: When you meet a word with more than one meaning, read the whole sentence. Ask yourself: does this make sense as an animal, or as food? Then check your choice by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: «Crabs» means sea or shore animals with a hard shell, ten legs and two big claws.
fact: Crabs walk sideways, and they are often found in rock pools.
fact: Crabs are crustaceans, like lobsters and shrimps.
fact: Crabs have an outer skeleton called an exoskeleton, and they shed it as they grow.
fact: «Crabs» can also mean the meat of these animals, eaten as food. Phrases to know: «rock pool crabs», «hermit crabs», «crab legs».
exercise: «Mia found three crabs in the rock pool.» What are crabs in this sentence? | Plants that grow on rocks | Pieces of seaweed | *Sea animals with a hard shell and two big claws | Small fish
exercise: «We had crab legs for dinner at the seaside café.» What are crabs in this sentence? | Boats in the harbour | *Food, the meat of these animals | Stones on the beach | Sandcastles
exercise: Which body part do crabs use to pinch and hold things? | *Claws | Tails | Wings | Antennae
test: Which is a safe way to pick up a crab in a rock pool? | *Pick it up gently from behind and mind the claws | Grab it quickly from the front | Put it in your pocket | Throw it onto the sand
test: «The crab walked sideways across the sand.» What is special about how crabs walk? | *They walk sideways | They swim on their backs | They walk backwards | They fly over the rocks
exam: What do crabs shed as they grow? | *Their hard outer shell | Their legs | Their eyes | Their claws
